s \n\nGovernment \nCounterparts \n\nService \nproviders \n\n1.  Assess the clarity of outcomes, the TOC and the alignment of planned programme efforts and strategies to the TOC – as well as to  the \n\nregional and country context, and UNICEF’s Strategic Plan. \n\n1.1  How  relevant  is  the  CLECSAP  in  relation  to  development  plans  of  the \ncountry and of the region? \n\n✓  ✓ \n\n✓ \n\n✓ \n\n1.2 How does the Programme align with UNICEF Global Strategic Plan and with \nspecific guidance on child labour? \n\n1.2.1 Do you think it addresses all the key strategies recommended to address \nchild labour? \n\n✓  ✓ \n\n1.2.2  Do  you  think  it  fosters  innovation  in  thinking  and  programming  about \nchild labour?  \n\n1.3 What do you think is going to be the long-term impact of the Project? How \nis the Programme going to make a difference for children (direct or indirect)? \n\n1.3.1 Do you think the benefits will last? In which ways?  \n\n1.4 What are the most relevant features of the Programme from the strategic \npoint of view, and what are the major challenges? \n\n1.4.1 Where do you see the  added value of UNICEF’s intervention strategies \nrelated  to  this  Programme  (policy  advocacy  and  upstream  work;  capacity \ndevelopment; knowledge brokering and knowledge management; awareness \nraising and community mobilization)? \n\n1.4.2 How do you see the Programme linked to interventions of other sectors \nthat would have an impact on the reduction/elimination of child labour?  \n\n1.4.3 Is there room to emphasize inter-sectoral, integrated cooperation in the \nProject? \n\n1.4.4  Is  there  room  for  knowledge  exchanges  between  the  countries \ninvolved/other countries in the region? On which specific components? \n\n1.4.5 Are there provisions to organise such exchanges? \n\n✓  ✓ \n\n✓ \n\n✓ \n\n✓  ✓ \n\n✓ \n\n✓ \n\n1.5  Is  the  TOC  for  CLECSAP  adequately  described?  Are  the  planned \n\nprogrammatic strategies and interventions adequate to me