  programme,  consider \nincluding disability status in the disaggregation \nof indicator 2.1 \n\nCLECSAP EVALUABILITY ASSESSMENT - FINAL REPORT \n\nPAGE 28 OF 62 \n\n \n \n\x0cOutput 2.1. Government-led structures, inclusive of civil society, \nare  strengthened  to  prevent  and  respond  to  the  economic \nexploitation  of  children/child  labour,  including  children  with \ndisabilities and children on the move \nOutput  indicator  2.1:  Number  of  States  (India)  and  Provinces \n(Pakistan) with a costed plan of action to address child labour/the \neconomic exploitation of children \nBaseline Ind: 1; Pk: 0  \nTarget Ind: 3; Pk: 1 \nMOVs \nUNICEF reporting; Electronic copies of the costed plans of action \nDisaggregation N/A \nOutput  2.2  Referral  system  is  established  to  prevent  and \nrespond to the  economic exploitation of children/child  labour, \nincluding children with disabilities and children on the move \nOutput Indicator 2.2: Number of districts in India and Pakistan with \nfunctional case management and referral mechanisms \nBaseline Ind: 1; Pk: 0  \nTarget Ind: 30; Pk: 1 \nMOVs \nUNICEF reporting; SOP manuals; Monitoring visits; Admin data \nDisaggregation \nThe  model  should  include  data  disaggregated  by  age,  gender, \ndisability and focus area \n\nOutput  2.3.  Mechanisms  (intercountry  and  interstate)  for \nvoluntary safe return/repatriation of children engaged in labour, \nincluding those with disabilities are in place (India) \nOutput  Indicator  2.3:  Number  of  States  in  India  with  inter-state \nmechanisms for voluntary/safe return/repatriation \nBaseline Ind: 1 \nTarget Ind: 3 \nMOVs \nMoU  between  the  source,  transit  and  destination  States;  SOP \nmanual on coordination and information sharing \nDisaggregation \nThe  mechanism  should  include  data  of  source,  transit  and \ndestination States and type of exploitation \nOutcome  3:  Community-based  mechanisms  are  operational  to \nprevent  and  respond  