oss-cutting themes (Gender, Disability, Children on the move)? \n\n2.4.1 How can they be improved to reflect these? \n\n2.5  Are  indicators,  baselines  and  targets  appropriate  to  reflect  the  country-\nspecific work? \n\n2.5.1 Is there the need for some adjustments? \n\n2.6  Have  resources  been  adequately  allocated  to  allow  for  data  collection, \nmonitoring and evaluation? \n\n2.7 Are there any challenges in the cooperation with Government Counterparts \nfor the production of data and planned M&E exercises?  \n\n✓  ✓ \n\n✓ \n\n✓  ✓ \n✓ \n\n3.  Propose the required changes to make the overall programme more evaluable. \n3.1  Are  there  any  specific  changes  to  the  TOC,  the  overall  Programme  and  its \nstrategies,  the  implementation  arrangements,  the  allocation  of  resources,  the \nknowledge  management  system  that  you  would  suggest  to  make  the \nprogramme more effective and evaluable? \n\n✓  ✓ \n\n✓ \n\n✓ \n\n✓ \n✓ \n\nCLECSAP EVALUABILITY ASSESSMENT - FINAL REPORT \n\nPAGE 44 OF 62 \n\n✓ \n\n✓ \n\n✓ \n\n✓ \n✓ \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\x0cObjectives & Questions \n\nInterviewee category \n\nSemi-structured, open-ended questions \n\nRO \nCP Team \n\nCO \nCP Teams \n\nCO \nM&E teams \n\nGovernment \nCounterparts \n\nService \nproviders \n\n3.1.1  Do  you  think  that  the  programme  activities  should  be  adjusted  in \nconsideration  of  the  impact  of  CoViD19  on  the  socio-economic  situation  of \nfamilies and children? Please provide specific suggestions \n\nOutcome specific Questions \n\n3.2 Are there any specific changes suggested on the formulation of Outcomes \nand Outputs, and on indicators? \n\n3.3  Is  there  any  additional  evidence  work  that  the  CO  should  consider \nundertaking  to  complement/feed  into  the  Programme  implementation  and \nevaluation?  \n4.  Provide recommendations on the final evaluation’s design and methodology  \n4.1  What  should  be  the  purpose,  objectiv