 \n\nhigh degree \n\nDirection \nNationale du \nTravail, Ministère \ndu Travail  \n\nHowever as for \nmuch of the \napplication of the \ntheory, the INPS \nis well in advance \nof the project.   \n\nNo concrete \nresults as yet \n\nNot aware that the \nproject had already \ncome to its end  \n\ncontinue – with \nsome financial \nsupport by the \nILO.   \n\nILO should go \nover and above \nthe theory \n(“intellectual \ncapital”) now and \nshould focus on \nsupporting \nconcrete actions, \nby assisting the \ntripartite partners \nin developing their \n“dispositifs”. \n\nNow there is \ngood knowledge \non the rights and \nthe duties of the \nmigrants, which \nhelps to provide \nmore effective \nassistance to \nmigrants and \ntheir families.  \n\nIt is a little early \nto expect real \nand lasting \nimpact \n\nWere informed that \nthe project had ended, \nbut could have a \npossible follow up \n\n“The hope is positive!” \n\nConsolidate what \nhas already been \nachieved and \nsupport us in \nimplementing \nconcrete projects.   \n\nPlease send us \nthe evaluation \nreport.  \n\nIf there is a \nsecond phase, the \nmessage and the \nobjectives should \nbe much more \nclear. The ILO \nshould show its \ninternational \nindependence in \nrelation to the \nstance of the \nEuropean Union.  \n\nThe project \nduration was too \nshort and because \nit has not been \nfinalized properly, \nthis has an impact \non the \nsustainability of \nthe results.  \n\nWe knew from the \nbeginning that and \nwhen the project \nwould come to an \nend. It leaves a taste \nof non-achievement.  \n\nAlthough we knew \nthat the project had \ncome to an end, it \nwas very abruptly.  In \nCasablanca we were \nclearly working in the \nbelieve that there \nwould be another \nphase (ref. the Casa \n\nConseil National \ndu Patronat du \nMali (CNPM) \n\nMedium \ndegree \n\nMedium \ndegree \n\nThe real impact \nhas been : \n\nNow the \n“employers” are \npart of the \ndiscussion on \nlabor migration – \nand should be! \n\n54\n\n \n \n\x0cOrganisation \n\nDegree of \nknowledge \non project \n\nDegree of \ncollaboratio\nn with \nproject \n\nEstimated \nimpact of \nproject \n\nUnderstanding of \n“end project” \n\nMessage to ILO \n\nUnion Nationale \ndes Travailleurs \ndu Mali (UNTM) \n\nHigh degree  High degree \n\nMedium to \nhigh degree \n\nMedium to \nhigh degree \n\nDirection \nNationale de \nl’Emploi, \nMinistère de \nl’Emploi et de la \nFormation \nProfessionnelle  \n\nRecommendations)  \n\nWe were aware of the \nproject’s end and that \nan evaluation was \nneeded to see if \nanother phase would \nbe needed.  In \nNouakchott we \nformulated a motion \nfor the project to be \ncontinued.   \n\nWe were informed \nabout the end of the \nproject and that an \nevaluation should take \nplace.  \n\nIt should end more \nserenely by better \ninforming the \npartners.   \n\nPlease continue.  \nTraining should \nnow be more \nspecific and be \nprovided to lower-\nlevel cadres.  Also \nsupport should be \nprovided to \nconcrete projects \n(examples \nprovided). \n\nMigration statistics \nshould get \nparticular attention \nin the future.   \n\nThe UNTM should \nbe assisted in \ncontact with \nworkers unions in \nEuropean \ncountries.  \n\nIf a second phase \nis envisaged, the \nproject should \nenter into \nbecoming more \n“practical”. Both \nILO projects \nshould be merged.   \n\nThe “employers” \nwork more \nintensively \ntogether with the \nother partners on \nthis issue.  \n\nThe project has \npermitted the \nUNTM to be \nstronger (have \nmore capacity) in \nthis field. A good \nexample is the \nknowledge \nacquired on \nmigration and \nlegislation, which \nis being put into \npractice now.  .  \n\nAlso there are \nnow regular \ncontacts with \nworkers unions in \nother countries in \nthe region.  \n\n90% has been \nachieved  \n\nLabor migration \nhas instead of \nbeing treated in a \nad-hoc manner, \nhas now become \nmore part of the \ngovernment’s \npolicy.  This is \ndone in a more \nconcerted \nmanner.   \n\nThe project has \nhelped \nenormously in \nbuilding \nknowledge.  \n\nNow “migration” \nhas been \nincorporated in \nthe national \nemployment \n\n55\n\n \n\x0cOrganisation \n\nDegree of \nknowledge \non project \n\nDegree of \ncollaboratio\nn with \nproject \n\nEstimated \nimpact of \nproject \n\nUnderstanding of \n“end project” \n\nMessage to ILO \n\nAgence National \npour l’Emploi \n(ANPE) \n\nLow to \nmedium \ndegree \n\npolicy.   \n\nIt helped us to be \nbetter oriented, \nand that is all. It \nremained rather \nsuperficial and \nnever sufficiently \nconcrete.  \n\nLow to \nmedium \ndegree \n(never \ninvited for \nmeetings / \ntraining \noutside Mali)  \n\nIt is understood that \nthe project is still \nongoing.   \n\nVery useful \nproject, but the \nANPE has not \nreally benefited \nfrom the \n“amélioration des \ncapacities \ninstitutionnelles…”  \nPlease help us to \ndevelop  a \nconcrete capacity \nin our work to offer \nservices to labor \nmigrants.   \n\nMOROCCO  \n\nOrganisation \n\nMinistère de \nl’Emploi et de la \nFormation \nProfessionnelle \n\nDegree of \nknowledge \non project \n\nDegree of \ncollaboration \nwith project \n\nEstimated \nimpact of \nproject \n\nUnderstanding \nof “end project” \n\nMessage to ILO \n\nHigh degree  High degree \n\nThe regional \nmeeting in \nCasablanca (April \n2010) was at the \nsame time an \nend-of-project \nmeeting as well \nas a planning \nworkshop.  \nTherefore the \nunderstanding \nwas that there \nwould be a \nsecond Phase.    \n\nThe financial means \nwere too limited for \nachieving concrete \nlasting results in such a \nlarge region.   \n\nThe ILO should \ncapitalize on earlier \nprojects and \nachievements (ref. \nproject 2004-2006). \n\nA second Phase should \nfocus on the concrete \nneeds for Morocco, \nalready identified during \nthis project.   \n\nSee further the not \nachieved actions in the \nprevious column for \nwishes during a second \nPhase. \n\nThe ILO is a very \nimportant international \nactor in the field of labor \nmigration (a “Chef de \nFile”), but it should now \n\nThe project has \nhelped to identify \nthe needs of the \nvarious actors in \nMorocco in this \nfield and \nprovided a useful \n“road map”.   \n\nThe project has \nnot been able to \nestablish on \nnational level a \nstrategic “veille” \nand on regional \nlevel a lasting \nnetwork.  \n\nNor has the \nratification of the \nBIT conventions \non Migration and \nLabor been \nachieved. \n\n56\n\n \n \n\x0cOrganisation \n\nDegree of \nknowledge \non project \n\nDegree of \ncollaboration \nwith project \n\nEstimated \nimpact of \nproject \n\nUnderstanding \nof “end project” \n\nMessage to ILO \n\nMinistère \nchargé de la \nCommunauté \nMarocaine \nRésidant à \nl’Étranger \n\nHigh degree  High degree \n\n(still needs \nconfirmation \non a number \nof activities in \nwhich the \nministry has \nparticipated)  \n\nMedium  \ndegree  \n\nMedium \ndegree \n\nFédération \nDémocratique \ndes Travailleurs \n(FDT) \n\nsupport its partners with \nconcrete projects based \non well-identified priority \nneeds.  Therefore, a \nsecond Phase should \nstart with a thorough \nneeds assessment \nmission.  \n\nBuilding institutional \ncapacity takes time.  \nAfter this phase of \nenlightenment, we now \nneed to move into \naction!  \n\nWhat is needed now is \nsupport to two actions: \n\n1. Technical assistance \nby a “informaticien \njuriste” in giving \nconcrete form to and  \nimplementing the “Veille \nJuridique”. \n\n2. Focused training on \nhow to operate the \n“Veille Juridique” \n\n1. Continue to support \nus with expertise in this \nfield \n\n2. Organize other \nworkshops where things \nare more profoundly \nstudied and discussed \n\n3. Help us to develop \ntraining for our “cadres” \nand allow us to learn \nfrom good practice \nelsewhere \n\n4. Support Morocco to \ncreate a national \nconsultative platform in \nthis field \n\nWe are aware of \nthe fact that the \nproject has come \nto its end.  \nHowever there \nwas always made \nreference to the \n“First Phase”, so \nnaturally we \nbelieve that there \nwill be a “Second \nPhase”.   \n\nAwareness of the \nproject ending, \nhowever no \nknowledge on \nany follow up.   \n\nAn inventory on \nlegal issues \nrelated to labor \nmigration and \nthe formulation \nof a “Veille \nJuridique” for \nMorocco and \ndestination \ncountries. \n\nThere has been \nsome impact in \nMorocco in the \nfield of \ninstitutional \ncapacity \nbuilding, but only \non the \ntheoretical level \n(increased \nknowledge and \nunderstanding).  \n\nThe issue of \nlabor migration \nhas been put on \nthe national \nagenda of \nworkers unions \nin Morocco \n\nA small network \nof resource \npersons has \nbeen developed \n– about 3 to 4 \nper national \nunion \n\nThe Congress of \nthe FDT has – \nfor the first time \n– an agenda \npoint (and a \ndocument) on \n\n57\n\n \n\x0cOrganisation \n\nDegree of \nknowledge \non project \n\nDegree of \ncollaboration \nwith project \n\nEstimated \nimpact of \nproject \n\nUnderstanding \nof “end project” \n\nMessage to ILO \n\nlabor migration \nincluded  \n\nLow degree \n\nTo be \ndiscounted  \n\nThe impression \nwas that the \nproject had just \nbegun… \n\nThe FCMCIS considers \nit has not been a \npartner in this project \n\nFédération des \nChambres \nMarocaines de \nCommerce, \nd’Industrie et de \nService \n(FCMCIS) \n\nVery low \ndegree, \nreceived a \nletter to be \ninvited to \ntake part in \nthis \nevaluation, \nbut this was \nnot \nunderstood  \n\n58\n\n \n \n \n \n\x0cThursday, \n16.09 \n\nThursday, \n16.09 \n\nThursday, \n16.09 \n\nThursday, \n16.09 \n\nAnnex B.  List of people met  \n\nDate \n\nNames and titles of persons met  \n\nOrganisation / unit \n\nRelation with projet \n\nGENEVA ILO HQ \n\nThursday, \n16.09  \n\nMs  Patricia ISIMAT-MIRIN \n\nILO \n\nProject Coordinator \n\nBy Skype \n\nMr.   Gugsa Yimer FARICE \n\nILO / Regional Office for Africa   Senior Monitoring 